# state: returning   (classifier-path opening on the kept profile; the 0.5 release soak, #433)
# Grabbed by the Ghoulies (4D530053), classifier path: `drive generic`
# replaces ghoulies.returning.route's blind opening (the book, the title
# page, slot 1 "My Game", Play, the storybook cards) and marks gameplay
# itself once play is confirmed in the Grand Hallway. The classifier has a
# recorded path for this title on the Nova (pathknow/paths/4D530053.json,
# 2026-10-02: gameplay in 2.35 min). drive never presses START in live
# play, which matters here: START in the hallway opens the pause menu.
#
# DOES NOT REACH PLAY YET (Nova, 2026-10-12, run 1-1791836906-lane.local-2003337):
# the title is named at 33.7 s and START pressed, then the "Choose A Game"
# slot menu reads main_menu 0.67, under the generic profile's 0.70 menu
# floor, for 91 s: ROUTE FAIL unknown. Over ghoulies.returning's 17 frames
# of the same opening (1-1791826297-lane.local-4125680) pathclass reads the
# slot menu at 0.57-0.82 and the Grand Hallway's play at 0.58-0.75
# `gameplay`, under the 0.85 gameplay floor, so even past the menus drive
# would never mark play. Use ghoulies.returning.route until pathclass names
# this title's menus and play above those floors.
#
# The play loop is ghoulies.route's, unchanged: walk with the left stick,
# hold the right stick to attack in four directions, A for tutorial cards.
drive generic 480 mark
repeat forever {
    axis LY min
    wait 1.5
    axis LY mid
    axis RX max
    wait 1
    axis RX mid
    axis LX max
    wait 1.5
    axis LX mid
    axis RY min
    wait 1
    axis RY mid
    axis LY max
    wait 1.5
    axis LY mid
    axis RX min
    wait 1
    axis RX mid
    axis LX min
    wait 1.5
    axis LX mid
    press A 200
    wait 0.5
}
